.TH DESKTOP_INSTALLER 1 "2026-10-05" "desktop_installer 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
desktop_installer \- add .desktop shortcuts of installed deb/snap packages to your desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B desktop_installer
.br
.B dtier
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B desktop_installer
scans all installed
.BR deb (5)
and
.B snap
packages, lists their
.B .desktop
files, and lets you add selected shortcuts to your desktop with a single click.
.PP
It automatically adds executable permissions and, on GNOME, marks the shortcut as trusted.
No
.B sudo
is required — everything runs with the current user's privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.SH USAGE
.TP
1.
Switch to the
.B deb
or
.B snap
tab.
.TP
2.
Use the sort dropdown to choose a sorting order.
.TP
3.
Check the packages you want to add.
.TP
4.
Click
.B Add
at the bottom right.
.TP
5.
If a file with the same name already exists on the desktop, choose
.BR overwrite ,
.B rename
or
.BR skip .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/*.desktop
Source of deb package shortcuts.
.TP
.I /var/lib/snapd/desktop/applications/*.desktop
Source of snap package shortcuts.
.TP
.I ~/Desktop
Target directory (resolved via XDG user dirs).
